{"tool_name":"hsmrf","contents":["biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:hsmrf"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"HSMRF","home":"http://github.com/afmagee/hsmrfbdp","summary":"Locally adaptive Bayesian birth-death model successfully detects slow and rapid rate shifts.\n\nCode for our work developing and characterizing the HSMRF priors for birth-death processes.\n\nThis repository contains code for analyses from \"Locally adaptive Bayesian birth-death model successfully detects slow and rapid rate shifts\" (Magee et al. 2019). In the directory 1_simulation_study is code for simulating a number of trees under a time-dependent birth-death process, inferring diversification rates under the HSMRF-based and GMRF-based models, and processing those results. In the directory 2_empirical_analyses is code for the empirical analyses presented in the manuscript. Both directories contain more extensive readme files.","addition_date":"2020-01-14T09:44:34Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-12T14:30:22.984501Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:HSMRF","edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Modelling and simulation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2426"},{"term":"Phylogenetic tree analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0324"},{"term":"Statistical inference","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3658"}]}],"name":"HSMRF","owner":"Pub2Tools","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/853960","type":["Preprint"]},{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pcbi.1007999","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Infectious disease","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3324"},{"term":"Phylogeny","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0084"},{"term":"Public health and epidemiology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3305"},{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:hsmrf/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creat